[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Advanced Networking in Flutter: Dio, Interceptors, WebSockets, and Serialization"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Building production-grade Flutter applications requires a robust architecture for managing network requests, authenticating users, handling real-time data streams, and mapping complex JSON payloads to strongly-typed Dart objects. In this tutorial, we will explore how to integrate Dio for HTTP requests, utilize Interceptors for global error handling and authentication, maintain real-time bi-directional communication with WebSockets, and achieve high-performance data serialization using json_serializable."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Setting Up Dependencies"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To begin, add the required networking and serialization packages to your pubspec.yaml file. We will use dio for HTTP operations, web_socket_channel for real-time streams, and json_annotation alongside build_runner for compile-time serialization."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"dependencies:
  flutter:
    sdk: flutter
  dio: ^5.4.0
  web_socket_channel: ^2.4.0
  json_annotation: ^4.8.1

dev_dependencies:
  build_runner: ^2.4.8
  json_serializable: ^6.7.1"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. High-Performance Data Serialization"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Manual JSON parsing using Map<String, dynamic> is prone to runtime errors. By using json_serializable, we can map JSON data directly to robust Dart classes safely and efficiently."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:json_annotation/json_annotation.dart';

part 'user_model.g.dart';

@JsonSerializable()
class UserModel {
  final int id;
  final String name;
  final String email;

  UserModel({required this.id, required this.name, required this.email});

  factory UserModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) => _$UserModelFromJson(json);

  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() => _$UserModelToJson(this);
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Configuring Dio and Interceptors"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Dio is a powerful HTTP client for Dart, supporting interceptors, global configuration, FormData, request cancellation, and file downloading. Interceptors allow you to intercept requests and responses before they are handled by the application, making them ideal for injecting authorization tokens, logging, and token refreshing."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:dio/dio.dart';

class DioClient {
  late final Dio dio;

  DioClient() {
    dio = Dio(
      BaseOptions(
        baseUrl: 'https://api.example.com',
        connectTimeout: const Duration(seconds: 5),
        receiveTimeout: const Duration(seconds: 3),
        headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      ),
    );

    dio.interceptors.add(AppInterceptor());
  }
}

class AppInterceptor extends Interceptor {
  @override
  void onRequest(RequestOptions options, RequestInterceptorHandler handler) {
    // Inject Auth Token dynamically
    String token = 'YOUR_SECURE_TOKEN_HERE';
    options.headers['Authorization'] = 'Bearer $token';
    print('REQUEST[${options.method}] => PATH: ${options.path}');
    return super.onRequest(options, handler);
  }

  @override
  void onResponse(Response response, ResponseInterceptorHandler handler) {
    print('RESPONSE[${response.statusCode}] => DATA: ${response.data}');
    return super.onResponse(response, handler);
  }

  @override
  void onError(DioException err, ErrorInterceptorHandler handler) {
    print('ERROR[${err.response?.statusCode}] => MESSAGE: ${err.message}');
    // Handle Token Expiration or Global Error States here
    return super.onError(err, handler);
  }
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Integrating WebSockets for Real-Time Data"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"While HTTP requests are ideal for request-response cycles, WebSockets provide persistent bi-directional communication channels. The web_socket_channel package simplifies connecting, listening to streams, and pushing payloads to a server."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:web_socket_channel/web_socket_channel.service.dart';
import 'package:web_socket_channel/web_socket_channel.dart';

class WebSocketService {
  late final WebSocketChannel channel;

  void connect() {
    channel = WebSocketChannel.connect(
      Uri.parse('wss://echo.websocket.events'),
    );
  }

  Stream<dynamic> get stream => channel.stream;

  void sendMessage(String message) {
    channel.sink.add(message);
  }

  void disconnect() {
    channel.sink.close();
  }
}"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"5. Best Practices and Summary"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always centralize your Dio configuration into a singleton or dependency injection provider (like get_it or Riverpod)."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use Interceptors for cross-cutting concerns like logging, caching, analytics, and auto-retrying failed network requests."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always close WebSocket channels inside the dispose method of your StatefulWidgets or ViewModel classes to prevent memory leaks."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage code generation tools such as build_runner to maintain type safety when dealing with massive JSON payloads."}]
